          is the residue of having been there, and you can&rsquo;t brief it
          into someone at the end.
        </p>
        <p>
          That participation is backed by a record. Because the reasoning
          behind every decision was captured as we went, not reconstructed at
          the close, what your team inherits includes the <em>why</em>, not
          just the <em>what</em>. They can ask why a thing is the way it is and
          get an answer, long after the people who decided it have moved on.
        </p>
        <p>
          And what they inherit is buildable&#8209;on. Not a black box we hand
          over and hope you never need to open, but architecture your team can
          read, a codebase they can change without fear, systems clean enough
          to carry the next initiative. Clean isn&rsquo;t an aesthetic here;
          it&rsquo;s the difference between owning the thing and being hostage
          to it.
        </p>
        <p>
          This runs against the grain of how most firms are built, and
          it&rsquo;s worth being blunt about why. For many consultancies your
          dependency is the business model: the reason you have to call them
          back is the reason they stay in business. Leaving you genuinely
          capable works against their own incentive, so, mostly without anyone
          deciding it, they don&rsquo;t. We treat the dependency you&rsquo;re
          left with as a defect in the work, not a feature of the contract.
        </p>
        <p>
          The result isn&rsquo;t just competence; it&rsquo;s ambition. Because
          you&rsquo;ve watched the scariest part of a real build get
          de&#8209;risked in weeks and ship, your sense of what&rsquo;s hard
          and what&rsquo;s reachable has been recalibrated against something
          real. The idea that got laughed out of the room starts to look like a
          plan, and this time you have the team and the ground to chase it.
          Whether the next thing needs us becomes a choice you make, not a
          position we engineered you into.
        </p>

        <h2 class="caps-heading">The Domains &amp; Capabilities at Work</h2>

        <h3 class="dom-label">Building</h3>
        <div class="cap">
          <button class="cap-head" aria-expanded="false">
            <span class="nm">Durable architecture</span>
            <span class="cap-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </button>
          <div class="cap-body">
            <div class="cap-body-in">
              <span class="r"
                ><span class="lbl">Why it&rsquo;s here</span>What you keep has
                to be buildable&#8209;on, not a sealed box. Architecture your
                team can read, a codebase they can change without fear, systems
                clean enough to carry the next initiative without calling us to
                open one we sealed.</span
              >
              <span class="r out"
                ><span class="lbl">Produces</span>Production&#8209;grade ground
                your team can own and extend on its own.</span
              >
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="dom-label">Continuity</h3>
        <div class="cap">
          <button class="cap-head" aria-expanded="false">
            <span class="nm">Capability transfer</span>
            <span class="cap-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </button>
          <div class="cap-body">
            <div class="cap-body-in">
              <span class="r"
                ><span class="lbl">Why it&rsquo;s here</span>Understanding is
                the residue of having been there. Your people are in the room
                when the hard calls get made (watching the tradeoffs, hearing
                why one path won) so they understand why the system works, not
                because we briefed them at the end.</span
              >
              <span class="r out"
                ><span class="lbl">Produces</span>A team that can operate and
                extend the system on its own judgment, not on our
                availability.</span
              >
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cap">
          <button class="cap-head" aria-expanded="false">
            <span class="nm">Context &amp; decision capture</span>
            <span class="cap-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </button>
          <div class="cap-body">
            <div class="cap-body-in">
              <span class="r"
                ><span class="lbl">Why it&rsquo;s here</span>Decisions,
                reasoning, risks and confidence can&rsquo;t live in a slide or
                one person&rsquo;s memory, or later work can&rsquo;t remember
                why earlier work decided what it did. This records them in one
                place as we go, increasingly with AI holding the threads.</span
              >
              <span class="r out"
                ><span class="lbl">Produces</span>A durable, queryable record
                that governs later decisions and carries the why forward,
                instead of being reconstructed.</span
              >
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="cap-note">
          These don&rsquo;t run as a loop; they accumulate. Every decision made
          in the open, every reason captured, every hour your people spend in
          the room compounds into a team that doesn&rsquo;t need us, which is
          the point. Ownership is the same principle turned outward: the
          capability leaves with you, and the last call we want to own is the
          one where you decide you can take it from here.
        </p>
      </main>
    </div>

    <script is:inline>
      const body = document.body;
      let flyer = null,
        ph = null,
        home = null,
        homeRect = null,
        panel = null;

      document.querySelectorAll(".godeep").forEach((a) =>
        a.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
          e.preventDefault();
          openSilo(a);
        }),
      );
      document
        .querySelectorAll(".silo-back")
        .forEach((b) => b.addEventListener("click", closeSilo));
      document.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
        if (e.key === "Escape" && body.classList.contains("silo-open"))
          closeSilo();
      });

      document.querySelectorAll(".cap-head").forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener("click", () => {
          const item = btn.closest(".cap");
          if (!item) return;
          const isOpen = item.classList.toggle("open");
          btn.setAttribute("aria-expanded", isOpen ? "true" : "false");
        });
      });

      function openSilo(btn) {
        const col = btn.closest(".col");
        const target = document.getElementById("silo-" + btn.dataset.silo);
        if (!col || !target || flyer) return;
        const r = col.getBoundingClientRect();
        flyer = col;
        home = col.parentNode;
        homeRect = r;
        ph = document.createElement("div");
        ph.style.height = r.height + "px";
        ph.className = "fly-ph";
        home.insertBefore(ph, col);
        body.appendChild(col);
        col.classList.add("flying");
        col.style.top = r.top + "px";
        col.style.left = r.left + "px";
        col.style.width = r.width + "px";
        col.style.maxHeight = r.height + "px";
        panel = target;
        panel.scrollTop = 0;
        panel.classList.add("open");
        body.classList.add("silo-open");
        requestAnimationFrame(() =>
          requestAnimationFrame(() => {
            col.classList.add("ref-mode");
            col.style.top = "72px";
            col.style.left = "44px";
            col.style.width = "320px";
            col.style.maxHeight = "150px";
          }),
        );
      }

      function closeSilo() {
        body.classList.remove("silo-open");
        if (panel) {
          panel.classList.remove("open");
          panel = null;
        }
        if (!flyer || !ph) return;
        const col = flyer,
          placeholder = ph,
          homeParent = home,
          r = homeRect;
        flyer = null;
        ph = null;
        col.classList.remove("ref-mode");
        col.style.top = r.top + "px";
        col.style.left = r.left + "px";
        col.style.width = r.width + "px";
        col.style.maxHeight = r.height + "px";
        setTimeout(() => {
          col.classList.remove("flying");
          col.removeAttribute("style");
          delete col.dataset.tier;
          homeParent.insertBefore(col, placeholder);
          placeholder.remove();
        }, 950);
      }

      // ── Thinking-orb, ported from the homepage hero (ported from
      // thinking-orbs engine/web.ts): a constellation of nodes on a
      // slowly-spinning sphere wires itself, drawn small here as a mark
      // above the opening line. ──
      function initStoryOrb() {
        const el = document.getElementById("storyOrbCanvas");
        if (!el || el.dataset.init) return;
        el.dataset.init = "1";

        const SIZE = el.offsetWidth;
        if (SIZE < 10) return;

        const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;
        el.width = SIZE * dpr;
        el.height = SIZE * dpr;

        const ctx = el.getContext("2d");
        if (!ctx) return;
        ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);

        const COLOR = "#E75437";
        const SIGNAL_COLOR = "#F4845F";
        const cx = SIZE / 2;
        const cy = SIZE / 2;

        const nodeN = 80;
        const thr = 0.68;
        const nodeR = 2,
          nodeRDepth = 2.8;
        const signals = 8;
        const lineW = 0.5;
        const SPEED = 1.8;
        const spread = 1;
        const ORB_R = (SIZE / 2) * 0.8 * spread;
        const rs = Math.pow(SIZE / 600, 0.3);

        function frac(x) {
          return x - Math.floor(x);
        }
        function lerp(a, b, f) {
          return a + (b - a) * f;
        }
        function hashD(a, b) {
          const h = Math.sin(a * 12.9898 + b * 78.233) * 43758.5453;
          return h - Math.floor(h);
        }
        function vnoise(x, y) {
          const xi = Math.floor(x),
            yi = Math.floor(y);
          let fx = x - xi,
            fy = y - yi;
          fx = fx * fx * (3 - 2 * fx);
          fy = fy * fy * (3 - 2 * fy);
          const a = hashD(xi, yi),
            b = hashD(xi + 1, yi),
            c = hashD(xi, yi + 1),
            d = hashD(xi + 1, yi + 1);
          return a + (b - a) * fx + (c - a) * fy + (a - b - c + d) * fx * fy;
        }
        const GOLDEN = Math.PI * (3 - Math.sqrt(5));
        function fibDir(i, n) {
          const y = 1 - (2 * (i + 0.5)) / n;
          const rad = Math.sqrt(1 - y * y);
          const a = i * GOLDEN;
          return [rad * Math.cos(a), y, rad * Math.sin(a)];
        }
        function makeProj(yaw, tilt) {
          const st = Math.sin(tilt),
            ct = Math.cos(tilt),
            sy = Math.sin(yaw),
            cyw = Math.cos(yaw);
          return function (x, y, z) {
            const x1 = x * cyw + z * sy;
            const z1 = -x * sy + z * cyw;
            const y1 = y * ct - z1 * st;
            const z2 = y * st + z1 * ct;
            return [cx + x1 * ORB_R, cy - y1 * ORB_R, z2];
          };
        }

        const reduced =
          window.matchMedia &&
          window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
        const startT = performance.now();

        function frame(t) {
          ctx.clearRect(0, 0, SIZE, SIZE);
          const pt = makeProj(t * 0.12, 0.32);

          const nodes = [];
          for (let i = 0; i < nodeN; i++) {
            const dir = fibDir(i, nodeN);
            const nx = dir[0] + 0.3 * (vnoise(i * 0.31 + 9, t * 0.24) - 0.5) * 2;
            const ny = dir[1] + 0.3 * (vnoise(i * 0.53 + 27, t * 0.21) - 0.5) * 2;
            const nz = dir[2] + 0.3 * (vnoise(i * 0.77 + 55, t * 0.27) - 0.5) * 2;
            const nl = Math.sqrt(nx * nx + ny * ny + nz * nz);
            nodes.push([nx / nl, ny / nl, nz / nl]);
          }

          ctx.lineWidth = Math.max(0.6, lineW * rs);
          for (let i2 = 0; i2 < nodeN; i2++) {
            for (let j2 = i2 + 1; j2 < nodeN; j2++) {
              const dx = nodes[i2][0] - nodes[j2][0];
              const dy = nodes[i2][1] - nodes[j2][1];
              const dz = nodes[i2][2] - nodes[j2][2];
              const dist = Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy + dz * dz);
              if (dist >= thr) continue;
              const pa = pt(nodes[i2][0], nodes[i2][1], nodes[i2][2]);
              const pb = pt(nodes[j2][0], nodes[j2][1], nodes[j2][2]);
              const edepth = ((pa[2] + pb[2]) / 2 + 1) / 2;
              ctx.globalAlpha = (1 - dist / thr) * (0.3 + 0.55 * edepth);
              ctx.strokeStyle = COLOR;
              ctx.beginPath();
              ctx.moveTo(pa[0], pa[1]);
              ctx.lineTo(pb[0], pb[1]);
              ctx.stroke();
            }
          }

          const dots = [];
          for (let i3 = 0; i3 < nodeN; i3++) {
            const pn = pt(nodes[i3][0], nodes[i3][1], nodes[i3][2]);
            const depth = (pn[2] + 1) / 2;
            const pulse = 1 + 0.25 * Math.sin(t * 1.4 + i3 * 2.7);
            dots.push({
              x: pn[0],
              y: pn[1],
              z: pn[2],
              r: (nodeR + nodeRDepth * depth) * pulse * rs,
              color: COLOR,
              a: 0.25 + 0.75 * depth,
            });
          }
          for (let s = 0; s < signals; s++) {
            const seg = Math.floor(t * 0.55 + s * 7.31);
            const ai = Math.floor(hashD(seg, s * 3.1 + 1.7) * nodeN);
            const bi = Math.floor(hashD(seg, s * 5.7 + 4.2) * nodeN);
            if (ai === bi) continue;
            const f = frac(t * 0.55 + s * 7.31);
            const sx = lerp(nodes[ai][0], nodes[bi][0], f);
            const sy2 = lerp(nodes[ai][1], nodes[bi][1], f);
            const sz = lerp(nodes[ai][2], nodes[bi][2], f);
            const sl = Math.max(1e-6, Math.sqrt(sx * sx + sy2 * sy2 + sz * sz));
            const ps = pt(sx / sl, sy2 / sl, sz / sl);
            const sdepth = (ps[2] + 1) / 2;
            dots.push({
              x: ps[0],
              y: ps[1],
              z: ps[2],
              r: (nodeR * 1.5 + nodeRDepth * sdepth) * rs,
              color: SIGNAL_COLOR,
              a: 0.5 + 0.5 * sdepth,
            });
          }

          dots.sort((p, q) => p.z - q.z);
          for (let k = 0; k < dots.length; k++) {
            const dd = dots[k];
            if (dd.a < 0.02) continue;
            ctx.globalAlpha = dd.a;
            ctx.fillStyle = dd.color;
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.arc(dd.x, dd.y, Math.max(0.3, dd.r), 0, Math.PI * 2);
            ctx.fill();
          }
          ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
        }

        function tick() {
          if (!document.body.contains(el)) return;
          frame(((performance.now() - startT) / 1000) * SPEED);
          requestAnimationFrame(tick);
        }

        if (reduced) {
          frame(1.2);
        } else {
          requestAnimationFrame(tick);
        }
      }

      initStoryOrb();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
